    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:56c6e65b43bc09b8",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "f6d55dbebbd38697dc13dcd2e42de5b2886fe5f65182e843374cb01a0899097e",
      "text": "Breakfast. At the scheduled time, you will be transferred to the international airport for your flight home. You can add a visit to the Larco Museum on the way.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw6krd1q-6gkvrjmldy",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      }
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:2d7659d1c33868d8",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "28991f7325a4e04d229a7aa153f93bb9d27cde8996df61548c3f909b4a2cd112",
      "text": "The optional visit to the Larco Museum costs $65 per person.\n\nArchaeologist Rafael Larco Hoyle founded the museum in 1926. The collection is housed in an 18th-century colonial mansion built on the site of an earlier pre-Columbian structure. Around 45,000 objects introduce you to the civilisations that lived in Peru long before the Incas.\n\nThe galleries display ceramics, textiles, gold and silver pieces, ritual objects and archaeological finds. A dedicated section features Moche pottery, including pieces with erotic scenes that offer insight into ancient Peruvians’ ideas about life and fertility.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw6krd1q-6gkvrjmldy",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      }
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:7bb4eb34795c6110",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "0f1e6c953ffb2fcbc53f53deb459b53786897873ddaa5f7664699395dfec8d6c",
      "text": "After the visit, transfer to the airport for your international flight.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw6krd1q-6gkvrjmldy",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      }
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_alt:ea6a3f6f1979ab42",
